# Types Folder
# 
# Purpose: Define TypeScript types, interfaces, and type definitions
# 
# Best Practices:
# - Organize types by domain or feature
# - Use interfaces for object shapes that might be extended
# - Use types for unions, intersections, and computed types
# - Export types that are shared across multiple modules
# - Keep types close to where they're used when they're module-specific
# - Use descriptive names for types and interfaces
# - Document complex types with comments
# - Group related types in the same file
# - Use enums for fixed sets of values
# 
# Example structure:
# - ai.types.ts (AI-related types)
# - poll.types.ts (Poll-related types)
# - api.types.ts (API request/response types)
# - common.types.ts (shared/common types)

